rms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the two-writer barrier patches the shared `fsutil.os.replace` seam (where the converted sites' replace actually executes), not each caller module's `os.replace`, and confirm the barrier predicate discriminates the target file across the multiple converted sites.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a threading.Barrier(2) with monkeypatch.setattr on the module's own os.replace, gating only the target write'","Exemplar works only because the verdict cache hand-rolls replace inline: test_completion_verdict_cache.py:520 `real_replace = cvc.os.replace` / :528 `monkeypatch.setattr(cvc.os, \"replace\", ...)`","fsutil.py:93 `os.replace(tmp, path)` executes in fsutil's own namespace; converted sites call fsutil.atomic_write rather than replacing inline"],"finding":"The Step 3 / AC3 regression test copies the exemplar's monkeypatch idiom ('monkeypatch.setattr on the module's own os.replace'), but after conversion the six sites delegate to fsutil.atomic_write, so os.replace executes in the fsutil module namespace — patching each caller module's os.replace will not intercept the actual replace seam, so the barrier never gates the converted write.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f172ff0f9b78ffe98","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach Step 3 / AC3","norm_id":"n1897e5e195841efa","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Test author patches reconcile.os.replace / janitor.os.replace expecting to gate the write; the barrier is never hit because the real replace lives in fsutil, so the two-writer interleave the test intends never occurs and the GREEN assertion passes vacuously."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Patch `fsutil.os.replace` (the single seam all